WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.663 --> 00:00:05.080
(soft music)

00:00:16.455 --> 00:00:19.687
- It's obviously an
icon, for the mountain.

00:00:19.687 --> 00:00:21.520
Just the symbol of it.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:28.027
- You don't have a lot of
opportunity in life these days,

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.610
to have 10 or 12 minutes alone.

00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:39.916
- Some people think
when they come here and

00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:42.556
they ride the chair it's a lonely ride.

00:00:42.556 --> 00:00:45.723
I never really thought of it that way.

00:00:49.973 --> 00:00:52.593
- Mad River was founded by
a guy named Roland Palmedo

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:55.168
'cause he wanted to start
a ski area where sport and

00:00:55.168 --> 00:00:58.016
not money was gonna be
the overriding concern.

00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:00.676
He built the single chair here in 1948 and

00:01:00.676 --> 00:01:02.535
then someone figured out very quickly that

00:01:02.535 --> 00:01:05.515
a double chair was just as easy
to build as a single chair.

00:01:05.515 --> 00:01:07.392
The single chairs went
away very quickly and

00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:10.677
this thing has kinda hung
around for a long time.

00:01:10.677 --> 00:01:13.927
(soft, relaxing music)

00:01:31.392 --> 00:01:33.269
- You're forced to really focus on

00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:34.496
what's going on around you.

00:01:34.496 --> 00:01:37.679
To look down, just watch some
of the skiers having fun and

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:38.823
when you get up there you can

00:01:38.823 --> 00:01:41.906
look across the valley into New York.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:51.872
- As the ski industry's
changed over the years,

00:01:51.872 --> 00:01:53.231
this place hasn't.

00:01:53.231 --> 00:01:55.759
Everything that we do shouldn't work.

00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:57.359
But it does.

00:01:57.359 --> 00:01:58.871
There's not a lot of
ski areas in the world

00:01:58.871 --> 00:02:03.038
where the skiers are donating
money to build the lift.

00:02:07.572 --> 00:02:08.998
- There's something about like, you know,

00:02:08.998 --> 00:02:10.908
waiting in line in the corral and

00:02:10.908 --> 00:02:13.489
you're going back and forth,

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:14.976
and you're saying hi to people,

00:02:14.976 --> 00:02:17.815
you're carrying on multiple conversations.

00:02:17.815 --> 00:02:20.782
It's just a real friendly
vibe that, you know,

00:02:20.782 --> 00:02:22.506
it's not like a hashtag campaign.

00:02:22.506 --> 00:02:26.673
We're trying to create a
community that's already here.

00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:34.662
- Sitting on that single
chair is like coming home.

00:02:34.662 --> 00:02:37.579
(soft piano music)

